.SS noust auth oidc set
Add an identity provider, or change one: only the settings given change.
.TP
.B Arguments
.br
\fIname\fR
.TP
.B \-\-issuer
The provider's issuer URL, exactly as its tokens write it.
.TP
.B \-\-client\-id
The client id Noust is registered as.
.TP
.B \-\-client\-secret\-stdin
Read the client secret from standard input.
.TP
.B \-\-prompt\-secret
Ask for the client secret at a hidden prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-secret
Forget the stored client secret (a public client).
.TP
.B \-\-label
What the button says after 'Sign in with'.
.TP
.B \-\-scopes
Space separated; openid is always asked.
.TP
.B \-\-enable
Offer it on the sign\-in page.
.TP
.B \-\-disable
Stop offering it, and refuse its answers.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-email\-verified
Refuse a sign\-in whose e\-mail the provider does not vouch for (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-unverified\-email
Let in people whose e\-mail is not verified; it is then never used to find an account.
.TP
.B \-\-assume\-email\-verified
Treat an e\-mail the provider says nothing about as verified (Microsoft Entra, a managed directory).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-assume\-email\-verified
Never assume it (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-clock\-skew
Seconds of clock difference to forgive (0\-300).
.TP
.B \-\-provisioning
A first sign\-in: off (an administrator links people), invite, or auto (create the account).
.TP
.B \-\-default\-role
The role of an account that provisioning creates.
.TP
.B \-\-default\-team
The team a created account joins ('' for the default team).
.TP
.B \-\-default\-team\-role
Its role there.
.TP
.B \-\-link\-by\-email
Link a first sign\-in to the account of its verified e\-mail (only one with a second factor).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-link\-by\-email
Never link by e\-mail.
.TP
.B \-\-allowed\-domain
Only e\-mail addresses of this domain (repeat for several).
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-domains
Allow every domain again.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-amr
The provider must say it used one of these methods, such as mfa (repeat for several).
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-amr
Require no method.
.TP
.B \-\-groups\-claim
Where the token lists groups; nest with '>'.
.TP
.B \-\-group\-sync
Let groups decide roles and teams at every sign\-in.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-group\-sync
Stop letting groups decide.
.TP
.B \-\-map\-role
GROUP=ROLE: members get this role (repeat).
.TP
.B \-\-map\-team
GROUP=TEAM:ROLE: members join this team (repeat).
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-mappings
Forget every group mapping.
.TP
.B \-\-redirect\-uri
The callback address, when it cannot be worked out ('' to clear).
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

