.TP
.B Arguments
.br
\fIdatabase\fR
.TP
.B \-\-engine, \-e
Engine the database is on.
.TP
.B \-\-all
One policy for every database of the engine, those created later too.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-database
With \-\-all, a database to skip. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-schema
PostgreSQL schema to leave out of every dump. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-table
Table (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB) or collection (MongoDB) to leave out. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-schedule
hourly, daily, weekly, monthly or a systemd OnCalendar expression. Default: daily.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Scheduled dumps to keep here, or 'none'. Dumps taken by hand are never deleted. Default: 7.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-days
Days to keep a scheduled dump here, or 'none'. Default: 30.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-gb
The most the scheduled dumps kept here may weigh together, in gigabytes, or 'none'. The newest dump always stays, whatever its size. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-to
Send each dump to this backup destination, keeping COUNT, DAYS and GB there. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-format
PostgreSQL's dump format. custom (pg_dump \-Fc) by default.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-restore
Load each dump into a temporary database, and drop it, as proof it restores.
.TP
.B \-\-disable
Keep the settings but install no timer.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the policy as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

