.TP
.B Arguments
.br
\fIname\fR
.TP
.B \-\-host
The server's address or name.
.TP
.B \-\-port
Where its sshd listens. Default: 22.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-user
The account the credential is for: root, or an account with passwordless sudo. Default: root.
.TP
.B \-\-key\-file
A private key to log in with instead of a password. It is read, used once and forgotten.
.TP
.B \-\-ask\-passphrase
The key has a passphrase: ask for it, without echo.
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
Read the password from one line of standard input instead of asking for it.
.TP
.B \-\-host\-key\-fingerprint
The server's ed25519 host key fingerprint, confirmed some other way (the provider's console, ssh\-keygen \-lf on the server). Without it the fingerprint is shown and asked.
.TP
.B \-\-access
The most this central may do on the server. Default: admin.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-host\-access, \-\-no\-host\-access
Also let this central reach the host itself there (SSH keys, sshd, the firewall).
